# GitHub workflow (saurabh0392/ctx)

This is the verified, working process for getting changes onto GitHub here. Follow it exactly. Do not assume tools that are not present.

## Environment facts (checked, not guessed)

- Remote: `https://github.com/saurabh0392/ctx.git`. Default branch: `main`.
- **`gh` is NOT installed.** Never run `gh ...` expecting it to work, and never report a PR as "created" when you only have a link. If you genuinely need programmatic PR create/merge, ask the user before installing `gh`.
- `git push` already works over HTTPS through the macOS keychain. No token, no extra auth.

## Steps

1. **Ticket first.** A Linear `CTX-<N>` issue must exist before any code (see the linear-ticket-first rule). Reuse the ticket's `gitBranchName`.
2. **Branch** off the latest `main`: `saurabhsharan03/ctx-<N>-<short-slug>`.
3. **Commit, tight.** First line is `CTX-<N>: <concise, outcome-oriented summary>` (e.g. `CTX-43: ship with profile filtering off by default`). One or few commits per PR, not a pile.
4. **Push:** `git push -u origin HEAD`.
5. **Open the PR by handing over a one-click link** (because `gh` is absent):
   `https://github.com/saurabh0392/ctx/compare/main...<branch>?expand=1`
   PR title = `CTX-<N>: <summary>`. Body references the ticket and uses `Fixes CTX-<N>` when it fully closes it. Say plainly that the user needs to click it; do not pretend it is already open.
6. **Merging is the user's call.** PRs land as **merge commits** via the GitHub "Merge pull request" button. Do NOT merge into `main` yourself, and NEVER force-push `main`, unless the user explicitly asks.
7. **Close the loop in Linear:** update the ticket status and add a short note on what shipped, with the PR link attached.

## Don't

- Don't call `gh` blindly. Don't claim a PR exists when you only produced a URL. Don't squash, rebase, or force-push `main`. Don't commit or push unless asked to.
